---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Data Methodology & Provenance — CityClick"
  description="Audit trail and data methodology for CityClick. Verified sources including US Census Bureau ACS, BLS, USGS, Open-Meteo, EPA, and Federal Reserve FRED."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="space-y-4 mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
        <span>🔬</span> Provenance & Standards
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-[#152438] tracking-tight">
        Data Methodology & Sources
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        CityClick operates under a strict sourcing policy: a blank is better than a wrong number. Every metric rendered on our platform is tied to an official federal, state, or municipal database with verified vintage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-12 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm">
      <!-- 1. Demographics & Economics -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-[#152438] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>📊</span> Demographics, Income & Labor Force
        </h2>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200 space-y-3">
          <div>
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900">US Census Bureau — American Community Survey (ACS 5-Year)</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">Source Vintage: 2019–2023 ACS Public Release · Geographic Level: Census Incorporated Place / County FIPS</div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            Total resident population, 5-year growth trajectory, median household income (MHI), per capita income, and daytime commuter labor inflow ratios are compiled directly from official Census ACS tables.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-500">
            <strong>Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis (FRED API):</strong> County-level monthly unemployment rates (`LAUCN` series) and civilian labor force benchmarks updated directly from Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS) releases.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Commercial Underwriting & NAICS Saturation -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-[#152438] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>💼</span> 25-Trade NAICS Saturation Index
        </h2>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200 space-y-3">
          <div>
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900">US Census Bureau — ZIP Codes Business Patterns (ZBP)</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">Mathematical Model: Empirical Bayes Shrinkage Prior (m = 10,000 national baseline)</div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            To prevent statistical distortion in smaller communities while accurately measuring saturation in major metros, establishment density per 10,000 residents is smoothed using Empirical Bayes shrinkage against national trade priors across 25 primary NAICS retail and service categories.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            Commercial lease rates ($/sqft/year) reflect asking triple-net (NNN) commercial retail benchmarks reconciled against regional brokerage reports and county appraisal district commercial records.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Physical Geography, Terrain & Climate -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-[#152438] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🏔️</span> Terrain Elevation & Climate Normals
        </h2>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200 space-y-3">
          <div>
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900">USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP Point Query Service)</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">Spatial Accuracy: 1/3-arc-second (~10-meter) Digital Elevation Models (DEM)</div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            Precise municipal elevation above sea level is resolved using exact municipal centroid coordinates queried against the National Elevation Dataset (NED).
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-500">
            <strong>Open-Meteo Meteorological Normals:</strong> 30-year climate baselines resolving annual sunny days, peak summer temperatures, winter low envelopes, and annual precipitation.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Municipal Utilities & Drinking Water -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-[#152438] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🚰</span> Municipal Drinking Water & Public Safety
        </h2>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200 space-y-3">
          <div>
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900">EPA Safe Drinking Water Information System (SDWIS Envirofacts)</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">Public Water System Identification (PWSID) Tracking</div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            Every municipal profile references the primary active Public Water System ID (e.g. `TX2270001` for Austin Water, `AR0000208` for Hot Springs Village), primary source classification (groundwater aquifer vs surface water reservoir), and Safe Drinking Water Act compliance status.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Continuous Audit Commitment -->
      <section class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-[#152438]">Public Audit & Corrections Policy</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a municipal official, civil engineer, or local business owner and notice a changed permit fee, new utility district, or adjusted school boundary, submit verification evidence to our research desk at <a href="mailto:audit@cityclick.com" class="text-[#1D68F2] font-bold hover:underline">audit@cityclick.com</a>. Verified corrections update within 48 hours.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
